lts less accurate.\n- Expect to get wrong answers. This is not a performance assessment, but an adaptive diagnostic that is attempting to find the contour of your knowledge profile." #edb/ref 13194139533463 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186385969 "Methods of Proof: Placement Exam\n\n- Response time is factored into the scoring, but don't rush! What's most important is that you answer correctly any questions that you understand.\n- You can take a break in between questions. Each question is timed independently.\n- Exiting a question before answering it will result in the question being marked as incorrect.\n- If you don't know how to answer a question, click the **Don't Know** button. Guessing will only make the results less accurate.\n- Expect to get wrong answers. This is not a performance assessment, but an adaptive diagnostic that is attempting to find the contour of your knowledge profile." #edb/ref 13194139533463 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186385971 "In some singular value decomposition problems, we do not get all of the needed vectors from the usual formulas right away.\n\nThis happens, for example, when:\n\n- an eigenvalue is repeated, or\n\n- a singular value is zero, so the corresponding vector is not determined uniquely.\n\nIn these cases, we proceed as follows:\n\n- **Step 1.** Solve the system that defines the eigenspace (or orthogonal complement).  \n\nFor example, we solve an equation of the form\n\n$$\n(A^T A - \\lambda I)\\mathbf{v} = \\mathbf{0},\n$$\n\nor, when finding missing columns of $U,$ we solve orthogonality conditions such as\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{u}_1 \\cdot \\mathbf{u} = 0, \\qquad \\mathbf{u}_2 \\cdot \\mathbf{u} = 0.\n$$\n\n- **Step 2.** Write the general solution using free variables.  \n\nThis shows that there are infinitely many solutions. For example, the solution might look like\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{v} = x\\,\\mathbf{b}_1 + y\\,\\mathbf{b}_2,\n$$\n\nwhere $x$ and $y$ are free variables.\n\n- **Step 3.** Choose convenient vectors from the solution space.  \n\nWe usually choose simple values for the free variables to get easy vectors. These vectors should be linearly independent and, if possible, already orthogonal.\n\n- **Step 4.** Orthogonalize the chosen vectors if necessary.  \n\nIf the vectors are not mutually orthogonal, we apply the Gram–Schmidt process.\n\n- **Step 5.** Normalize the vectors.  \n\nAfter that, we divide each vector by its norm to obtain unit vectors.\n\nThese unit vectors form an orthonormal basis for the solution space, and they can be used as the needed columns of $V$ or $U.$\n\n**Note:** In these situations, there is usually *more than one correct answer*. Different choices of free variables can produce different orthonormal bases, so the resulting SVD is not necessarily unique. What matters is that the chosen vectors:\n\n- belong to the correct solution space,\n\n- are mutually orthogonal, and\n\n- have norm $1.$\n\nLet's see a concrete example." #edb/ref 13194139534512 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186405287 "**6.6 Surface Integrals**\n\nDue: 2026-11-19\nSource: [Macmillan Achieve](https://achieve.macmillanlearning.com/ihub/assessment/f188d950-dd73-11e0-9572-0800200c9a66/5a1db2a7-4295-4a4c-9dbb-ceb8b174a282/d49c94ff-8be8-4c47-a468-0e086815d133)\n\nStudy answers and explanations are authored additions, not publisher solutions.\n\n## Instructions\n\nUse exact symbolic notation and fractions as needed. Problems 8–9 omit the numerical constant density; study references use ρ₀ and explain unit density. Outward normals on their open paraboloids are interpreted relative to the naturally capped solids. Source: Sullivan 2e Calculus, W.H. Freeman. Unlimited attempts, no incorrect-attempt penalty; up to 50 days late at a 2% daily penalty." #edb/ref 13194139533506 #edb/ref 17592186045419] [17592186405290 "**6.4 Green’s Theorem**\n\nDue: 2026-10-29\nSource: [Macmillan Achieve](https://achieve.macmillanlearning.com/ihub/assessment/f188d950-dd73-11e0-9572-0800200c9a66/5a1db2a7-4295-4a4c-9dbb-ceb8b174a282/acfcfc0c-cb8c-4110-b65a-55fe3f15159f)\n\nStudy answers and explanations are authored additions, not publisher solutions.\n\n## Instructions\n\nGive exact answers using symbolic notation and fractions. Use Green’s theorem where required. For Problem 11, the reference answer uses the standard positive orientation of a region’s boundary; the platform prompt does not state it explicitly. Source: Sullivan 2e Calculus, W.H. Freeman. Unlimited attempts, no incorrect-attempt penalty; up to 50 days late at a 2% daily penalty." #edb/ref 13194139533506 #edb/ref 17592186045419] [17592186405294 "**6.5 Divergence and Curl**\n\nDue: 2026-11-05\nSource: [Macmillan Achieve](https://achieve.macmillanlearning.com/ihub/assessment/f188d950-dd73-11e0-9572-0800200c9a66/5a1db2a7-4295-4a4c-9dbb-ceb8b174a282/c2f7ce2a-abae-4f76-b153-1b5653abd0c5)\n\nStudy answers and explanations are authored additions, not publisher solutions.\n\n## Instructions\n\nUse exact symbolic notation and fractions as needed. Source: Sullivan 2e Calculus, W.H. Freeman. Unlimited attempts with no incorrect-attempt penalty; submissions up to 50 days late at a 2% daily penalty." #edb/ref 13194139533506 #edb/ref 17592186045419] [17592186405305 "**Math 255 — Written Homework 2**\n\nDue: 2026-10-08\nSource: [Original worksheet](/api/source?path=%2Fhome%2Fjake%2FDeveloper%2Fstudy%2Fvault%2FF26%2Fsource%2F255%2FWHW-2%2F255-WHW2.pdf)\n\nStudy answers and explanations are authored additions, not publisher solutions.\n\n## Instructions\n\nShow clear, neat supporting work or a written explanation for every problem. Some problems are graded for correctness; logical, organized progress can earn partial credit, but correct answers without supporting work do not earn full credit. Work on the printed worksheet, digitally on the PDF, or on separate paper with the same layout. Include first name, last name, and OSU student ID on the cover. Upload a single six-page PDF to Gradescope under **Written Homework 2**: cover followed by one page per problem, including blank problems. Scan printed work or photograph separate pages; combine multiple pages for a problem into one page before merging. Digital work already follows the template. Incorrect formatting receives 0. No due date is stated in the PDF." #edb/ref 13194139533506 #edb/ref 17592186045419] [17592186405336 "**6.8 The Divergence Theorem**\n\nDue: 2026-12-03\nSource: [Macmillan Achieve](https://achieve.macmillanlearning.com/ihub/assessment/f188d950-dd73-11e0-9572-0800200c9a66/5a1db2a7-4295-4a4c-9dbb-ceb8b174a282/3929e7f7-d086-490c-9ebd-e2b4a59f88cf)\n\nStudy answers and explanations are authored additions, not publisher solutions.\n\n## Instructions\n\nUse exact symbolic notation and fractions where needed. For flux problems, n is the outer unit normal and S is the entire boundary unless stated otherwise. Use the requested theorem or formula and show its application. Source: Sullivan 2e Calculus, W.H. Freeman. Unlimited attempts, no incorrect-attempt penalty; up to 50 days late at a 2% daily penalty." #edb/ref 13194139533506 #edb/ref 17592186045419] [17592186405338 "**1.1 Parametric Equations**\n\nSource: [Macmillan Achieve](https://achieve.macmillanlearning.com/ihub/assessment/f188d950-dd73-11e0-9572-0800200c9a66/5a1db2a7-4295-4a4c-9dbb-ceb8b174a282/1af7ea5c-56c7-4f8d-aaec-e540bb4b3c9e?actualCourseId=5a1db2a7-4295-4a4c-9dbb-ceb8b174a282)\nDue: 2026-10-01\nImported: 2026-10-01 · 6 questions\n\nStudy answers, explanations, and reference graphics are authored additions to the linked source." #edb/ref 13194139533506 #edb/ref 17592186045419] [17592186405400 "Source: [MTH341-WHW1.pdf](/api/source?path=%2Fhome%2Fjake%2FDeveloper%2Fstudy%2Fvault%2FF26%2Fsource%2F341%2FWHW-1%2FMTH341-WHW1.pdf)\nDue: 2026-10-07\n\nTextbook: [A First Course in Linear Algebra — Version 2017, Revision A](/api/source?path=%2Fhome%2Fjake%2FDeveloper%2Fstudy%2Fvault%2FF26%2Fsource%2F341%2FKuttler-LinearAlgebra-AFirstCourse-2017A.pdf), by Lyryx Learning, based on the original text by K. Kuttler. Exercise text reproduced from the CC BY textbook; see its license page.\n\nStudy answers, explanations, and reference graphs are authored additions to the linked textbook exercises.\n\n## Instructions\n\nPut your solutions on separate sheets of paper (8.5 × 11 inches or A4). Use the original assignment sheet as a cover sheet and fill in your name and student ID. Submit your homework on Canvas. The assignment sheet states that late homework is not accepted." #edb/ref 13194139533506 #edb/ref 17592186045419] [17592186405406 "**1.2 Calculus of Parametric Curves**\n\nSource: [Macmillan Achieve](https://achieve.macmillanlearning.com/ihub/assessment/f188d950-dd73-11e0-9572-0800200c9a66/5a1db2a7-4295-4a4c-9dbb-ceb8b174a282/2800fbc5-4e58-452a-89b1-afe688a3b8bf?actualCourseId=5a1db2a7-4295-4a4c-9dbb-ceb8b174a282)\nDue: 2026-10-01\nImported: 2026-10-01 · 10 questions\n\nStudy answers, explanations, and reference graphics are authored additions to the linked source." #edb/ref 13194139533506 #edb/ref 17592186045419] [17592186405417 "MTH 256 F 2026 Written Homework 1\n\nDate imported: 2026-09-30\nDue: 2026-10-02\n\nSource: [Original worksheet](/api/source?path=%2Fhome%2Fjake%2FDeveloper%2Fstudy%2Fvault%2FF26%2Fsource%2F256%2FWHW-1%2F256-WHW1.pdf)\n\nStudy answers, explanations, and reference graphics are authored additions to the linked source." #edb/ref 13194139533506 #edb/ref 17592186045419] [17592186405461 "Source: [MTH255-WHW-Week1_v1.pdf](/api/source?path=%2Fhome%2Fjake%2FDeveloper%2Fstudy%2Fvault%2FF26%2Fsource%2F255%2FWHW-1%2FMTH255-WHW-Week1_v1.pdf)\nDue: 2026-10-01\n\n## Instructions\n\nShow clear, organized work or a written explanation for every problem where required. Some problems are graded for correctness; an answer without supporting work does not earn full credit.\n\nYou may write on a printed copy, annotate the PDF digitally, or use your own paper with the same problem layout. Submit one seven-page PDF to **Gradescope → W